<title>LITHUANIA: LOANS AND DEPOSITS RISE IN COMMERCIAL BANKS.</title>
<headline>LOANS AND DEPOSITS RISE IN COMMERCIAL BANKS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deposits in Lithuania's commercial banks rose during the month of March to 5.0333 billion litas from 4.9665 billion litas, the country's central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bank also said in a statement that loans granted by commercial banks increased in March to 4.1659 billion litas from 4.0854 billion litas.</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40</p>
